Strata's CPU expert pool: where Impulse's copy went (One Engine P0, 2026-10-25).

Since One Engine P0 there is ONE copy of the pool: flashnext/src/kernels/cpu and flashnext/include (Strata's tree,
impulse/flashnext/IMPULSE.md), with Impulse's additions merged in. impulse/CMakeLists.txt builds impulse_pool from it, and
flashnext/CMakeLists.txt builds strata_kernels_cpu from it. This folder keeps only Strata's licence (LICENSE, the same text
as flashnext/LICENSE) and this record. impulse/third_party/ggml/ (ggml-common.h, identical to
flashnext/third_party/ggml/) went too.

Each line: the file's path here before P0 -> its path now (which version the one copy keeps). Checked bit for bit: both
trees' pool tests under STRATA_NO_NVFP4_VNNI / STRATA_NO_NVFP4_512, and every gate/up and down row function of the old
flashnext copy, the old Impulse copy and the merged copy on the same inputs (Q4_0, Q4_K/Q8_0, IQ3_XXS/IQ4_NL, a real
NVFP4 pack blob, Impulse's SwiGLU_ggml / GeGLU NVFP4 with per-job scales).

